# netsurf: a block restyled whole may hold floats and list markers (patch 420)
# Generated 2026-11-08
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 419)
#
# The census's largest decline after 419, "restyled block holds floats or
# list markers" (14 in r132; more since 417 sends attribute changes to the
# restyle paths): rte's float columns (6), google's body and list items
# (4), cnnlite's consent block of floats (2), archwiki's and google's
# list items with markers (list-style-type: none), stackoverflow's block
# holding a list.
#
# Patch 376 declined both: "an ancestor's float list may hold it" and "a
# list marker (its item's numbering)". Neither holds in this engine:
#  - a marker's number is worked out at layout (box_construct_marker:
#    "numerical list counters get handled in layout"), not from any
#    construction state a subtree rebuild would lose; html_rl_flex_restyle
#    lays the page out whole after the rebuild. CSS counters still decline
#    (374's guards, unchanged);
#  - floats: html_rl_flex_restyle empties every ancestor's float_children
#    before the old boxes are freed when the old subtree held floats; the
#    full layout right after builds each list again
#    (layout_block_context starts it empty).
#  - Still declined: a list marker with an image (its object is not
#    carried over by html_rl_relink_subtree, which walks children).
#
# Sites (scratch build): float/marker declines 14 -> 0 (rte 6, google 4,
# cnnlite 2, archwiki, stackoverflow); block subtrees restyled rte 63 ->
# 72, google 4 -> 12.
#
